# Mutation cases for "a computed type a `sce-static` document declares the
# processors of costs it no script engine" (docs/SCE_ACCEPTED_SUBSET.md §2.15, "A
# computed type"; docs/adr/0005, decision 3).
#
# Run with
# `scripts/mutate sce-build/tests/mutations/a_declared_computed_type_costs_a_static_document_no_engine.cases`.
#
# A `<send typeexpr>` is evaluated at run time under a script data model, and costs
# the machine its engine. Under `datamodel="sce-static"` it is lowered to the string
# it computes and held to the processors the document declares as `sce:types`, so
# the same attribute costs nothing. The analyzer's own unit test holds both halves:
# the static document has no `SendDynamicAttr` cause, and the ECMAScript one has. The
# mutant takes the first away and the machine is then one that needs an engine it was
# declared to have none of:
#
#   a computed type of a static document is counted as evaluated at run time.
#
# Anchors are literal slices of the source; an edit that moves one is reported
# INCONCLUSIVE with the anchor quoted, never as a pass.

mutation_tests -p sce-build --features cli --lib script_engine_analyzer::tests::a_declared_computed_type_costs_a_static_document_no_engine
mutation_targets sce-build/src/script_engine_analyzer.rs
mutation_oracles sce-build/src/script_engine_analyzer.rs

mutation_case "a computed type of a static document costs a script engine" <<'PY'
edit("sce-build/src/script_engine_analyzer.rs",
     "        || (!static_model && !action.typeexpr.is_empty())\n",
     "        || !action.typeexpr.is_empty()\n")
PY
